        {
            "type": "text-block",
            "label": "Problem",
            "heading": "Photo selection was all admin.",
            "content": "After a shoot, choosing photos usually means sending a Drive folder, waiting for screenshots or a list of file names typed by hand, then matching them up one by one. Clients get lost in folders, and photographers lose time on admin instead of editing.",
            "goals": [
                "Cut photo selection down to open, tap, send.",
                "Keep photos in the photographer's own Google Drive, with no re-uploading.",
                "Deliver picks where the conversation already lives: WhatsApp."
            ]
